      "side": 1,
      "message": "[From Jetski review] Soundness: Similar to `write_custom`, having safe `pub fn write_slice` and `pub fn write\u003cT: Copy\u003e` on `BigEnoughBuffer` allows safe functions given a `\u0026mut BigEnoughBuffer` to call them repeatedly and write past the reserved capacity without `unsafe`. Additionally, `write\u003cT: Copy\u003e` allows passing a `Copy` struct with padding bytes, copying uninitialized memory into the C++ `char[]` buffer (UB when later read by `str()` / `WriteToFile()`).\n\nSince only single-byte writes (`u8`) are needed right now, consider replacing `write\u003cT: Copy\u003e` with `write_byte(\u0026mut self, val: u8)` and marking the write methods `unsafe fn` (or keeping them private to this module).",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "dcc9633efe39e3c1b65bbba7b1e20c8c9a71ba82",
      "serverId": "c360c8e5-7aa8-3905-a7a0-810934766dac"
