      "side": 1,
      "message": "[From Jetski review] Soundness / double evaluation: `buf_write!` evaluates each `$arg` twice — once for `maximum_size(\u0026$arg)` and again for `write_to_buf(\u0026$arg, \u0026mut cursor)`. If safe code passes an expression with interior state or side effects (e.g. `iter.next().unwrap()`), the second evaluation can return a larger value than what was reserved, causing an out-of-bounds write (UB) from purely safe code.\n\nBinding the arguments once upfront in a `match` tuple avoids double evaluation (and using `checked_add` prevents size wraparound in release builds).",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "dcc9633efe39e3c1b65bbba7b1e20c8c9a71ba82",
      "serverId": "c360c8e5-7aa8-3905-a7a0-810934766dac"
