      "side": 1,
      "message": "[From Jetski review] Strict aliasing concern: `cur_` has type `char*`, and casting `\u0026cur_` (`char**`) to `uint8_t**` (`unsigned char**`) and modifying it through `*mut u8` on the Rust side violates C++ strict aliasing rules (the character-type aliasing exception does not extend to pointer-to-pointer types like `char**` vs `unsigned char**`, and `build/gen.py` does not pass `-fno-strict-aliasing`). Especially with cross-language LTO enabled in CL 28100, could we change `rw_buf_` / `cur_` / `end_` to `uint8_t*` (or use `c_char` on the FFI bridge) so no pointer-to-pointer `reinterpret_cast` is needed?",
      "isAi": true,
